WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:03.840
The men and women of Raqqa is Being Slaughtered
Silently

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:06.200
are real journalistic heroes.

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:12.040
They work in secret and under constant threat,

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:17.300
reporting on the depredations of ISIS in their
home city.

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:20.200
Some fled in fear for their own lives.

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:24.540
Even in exile, they are in no way safe.

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:28.380
The website Raqqa is Being Slaughtered Silently

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:33.360
publishes firsthand accounts of the war crimes
of ISIS in often horrific detail.

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:34.440
City of Ghosts,

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:38.820
a new documentary by Academy Award nominated
director Matthew Heineman,

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:42.120
tells the story of the citizen journalists
who risk their lives

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:47.449
to show the world the atrocities committed
by the Islamic State of Iraq and Syria.

00:00:47.449 --> 00:00:51.710
And after ISIS took over the city there really
was not any information going in

00:00:51.710 --> 00:00:52.710
or information going out.

00:00:52.710 --> 00:00:56.380
There were no western journalists there.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:58.780
They would be killed instantly.

00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:05.379
And so, you know, this group really provided
a service to the world

00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:10.140
to help understand the atrocities that were
being committed in their home town.

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:13.200
Which just happened to be the capital of the Islamic
State.

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:15.750
Basically we're working two groups.

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:20.260
The first group is operating in Raqqa and
there are 17 colleagues,

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:22.660
and we are almost 10 outside.

00:01:22.670 --> 00:01:29.969
So the first group, our team in Raqqa, they
take photos, videos,

00:01:29.969 --> 00:01:36.780
they send us the news, information, and they
send it to the second team outside,

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:42.360
and the second team publish it online, on
social media, on our website.

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:46.340
And at the same time we smuggle information
in,

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:49.899
because Raqqa is cut off from the entire world.

00:01:49.899 --> 00:01:54.620
There's like no satellites, no TV, mostly
there are no internet.

00:01:54.620 --> 00:01:58.930
So we spread a magazine inside Raqqa city,

00:01:58.930 --> 00:02:03.180
so our magazine has the same cover as the
ISIS magazine

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:06.659
to reach out the largest number of audience.

00:02:06.659 --> 00:02:12.110
So it's our main tool to educate the people
about the ideology of ISIS,

00:02:12.110 --> 00:02:14.030
about the risk of ISIS.

00:02:14.030 --> 00:02:16.320
I think one of the remarkable things about
the group

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:18.280
is that these guys didn't have to do this.

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:20.160
You know, they didn't have to become citizen
journalists,

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:24.300
they're all studying to become doctors and
lawyers and scientists,

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:28.000
but they chose to do this and this choice
came with enormous consequences.

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:13.420
I didn't want to shy away from the violence,

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:17.140
I didn't want to shy away from the reality,
the horror, the fear,

00:03:17.140 --> 00:03:20.360
that the citizens of Raqqa live with every single
day.

00:03:20.360 --> 00:03:23.800
On the other hand I didn't want people in
theaters to sort of run out

00:03:23.810 --> 00:03:25.790
because it was so extreme.

00:03:25.790 --> 00:03:30.260
And so, you know, very much tried to walk
that tight rope.

00:03:31.660 --> 00:03:36.360
But again, I don't think it would do justice
to this story, to the group,

00:03:36.370 --> 00:03:39.180
to all that they've been through to shy away
from this violence.

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:44.260
And I think it's, you know, important to show,
to help people empathize

00:03:44.260 --> 00:03:46.160
for what they have to live with every single
day.

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:55.040
For sure, like, to watch your colleagues or
your family members, your relatives,

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:57.620
are getting killed.

00:03:57.620 --> 00:04:00.020
It's like something not easy.

00:04:00.020 --> 00:04:04.120
And especially I was with my colleague who
watched the video

00:04:04.120 --> 00:04:06.540
the execution video of his father.

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:14.200
So I don't know how he's feeling now, and
he keep watching this video.

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:20.139
But like when I asked him he said that watching
this video give him more power

00:04:20.139 --> 00:04:21.799
to complete the work.

00:04:21.799 --> 00:04:28.509
So it was like a hard thing but watching this
videos or the video of our colleagues,

00:04:28.509 --> 00:04:34.300
our family members, it gives like more power

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:35.660
to complete  our work.

00:05:56.480 --> 00:05:58.840
I can't compare our group with ISIS.

00:05:58.840 --> 00:06:03.960
ISIS is like the media office in Decorah as
an example

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:10.160
is getting like a hundred thousand fifty five
dollars monthly to do their work,

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:11.940
and we were running out of funds.

00:06:11.949 --> 00:06:14.539
So they have all the equipment to shoot their
videos,

00:06:14.539 --> 00:06:17.360
And we are working with simple equipment.

00:06:17.360 --> 00:06:20.340
So first we can't compare about size,

00:06:20.340 --> 00:06:25.810
and then but even without all these funds
or even experience

00:06:25.810 --> 00:06:28.050
we were able to make a change.

00:06:28.050 --> 00:06:33.500
So and that's the reason ISIS started to target us specifically.

00:06:33.500 --> 00:06:36.520
You know in this world of sort of 'fake news'

00:06:36.520 --> 00:06:40.999
and where truth seems to be malleable, I think
there's not,

00:06:40.999 --> 00:06:45.229
there's no more important story to tell than
the story of people fighting for the truth,

00:06:45.229 --> 00:06:50.569
people seeking the truth, people risking their
lives to expose the truth,

00:06:50.569 --> 00:06:56.090
and, you know, that's one of the biggest motivations
for me to make this film,

00:06:56.090 --> 00:07:00.150
was to highlight the incredible work that
Aziz and his colleagues are doing.

00:07:00.160 --> 00:07:04.780
To some degree this film is an homage to journalism,
an homage to citizen journalism,

00:07:04.780 --> 00:07:06.880
an homage to fighting for the truth.

